__pycache__/
*.pyc
# The environments `uv run` installs this tree into: .venv on the floor, and one
# per interpreter under `make matrix`.
.venv*/

# Gate transcripts: one slot per gate, cleared per run, bounded by construction.
.gate-reports/

# Per-worktree scope marker tools/dev/agent-worktree.sh plants for the hooks to read.
.agent-scope

# Conveyor run state: where a `release`/`adopt` run got to. Working state, not a
# record — the record is the ledger row, which is tracked. Ignored because
# `tree-clean` is itself a step, so a TRACKED position file would be dirtied by
# the very run that checks the tree is clean. Losing it costs nothing: every
# check() is a question about the tree, so the next run re-derives the position.
.agentic-sdlc/
